>s
Small brook
The grounds of the Korenvliet estate end here at a small brook with slippery
banks, which blocks further passage to the south.  You could follow the brook
to the east where it flows into a lake.  Through some trees to the north you
can glimpse a flagstone patio, and there is a vast meadow to the west.


>e
Lakeshore
The small brook ends here and flows into a large lake.  Thick bushes block
passage along the shore.  You could follow the brook back to the west.


>e
Your rubber boat needs to be inflated first.


>inflate boat
You inflate the boat.  Now you're out of breath.


>e
Lake
You are in the middle of the lake.  The shore to the west is quite far away.
To the south, the lake opens out into waters known as the South Bay.

You see a rubber boat here.


>dive
You'll need to wear a snorkel in order to breathe under water.


>s
South Bay
This part of the lake is called the South Bay, famous for its fishing.  It's a
fairly deep part of the lake and the water is cold here.  From here, you could
go back north to the middle of the lake.

A salmon is splashing around in the water here.

You see a rubber boat here.


>take salmon
Taken.

(Your score has just increased by one point.)

>take snorkel
Taken.


>wear snorkel
Okay, you’re now wearing the snorkel.


>wear goggles
Okay, you’re now wearing the pair of swimming goggles.


>dive
You dive underwater.

South Bay (under water)
You are swimming underwater somewhere in the South Bay.  The water is very
cold.  The lake floor throws up clouds of mud as you pass by.  It seems
possible to swim north from here.  You also spot what looks like a tunnel in
the lake floor to the west.


>w
Underground stream
You are swimming in an underground stream.  This rocky passage is rather tight
and it's extremely dark here.  The stream continues to the east and west.


>w
Underground Cave
You are swimming in a small underground cave, filled completely with water.
It's extremely dark here.  An underground stream leads east.

An empty bottle is lying on the cave floor.


