>x drain
This drain seems to lead into a sewer pipe.  A person could probably squeeze
into it.  It’s open.


>d
With some effort, you squeeze yourself feet first into the drain.

Sewer
You are inside the north end of a dimly lit, round concrete sewer pipe.  The
pipe continues to the south.  There is a drain here, leading up.


>s
Curve in the sewer
You are inside a round concrete sewer pipe.  It's a tight fit, and it's very
dark here.  The pipe curves from the north to the east.


>e
Fork in the sewer
You are inside a round concrete sewer pipe.  It's a tight fit, and it's very
dark here.  The pipe forks here, leading off to the north, south and west.


>s
Curve in the sewer
You are inside a round concrete sewer pipe.  It's a tight fit, and it's very
dark here.  The pipe curves from the north to the west.


>w
Sewer
You are inside a dimly lit, round concrete sewer pipe.  The pipe continues to
the east as well as downwards.  There is a drain here, leading up.


>d
Sewer
You are at the end of a dimly lit, round concrete sewer pipe.  The pipe
continues upwards from here.  There is a drain here, leading west.


>w
With some effort, you squeeze yourself head first through the drain.

East wine cellar
Korenvliet's wine cellar is large and musty.  Arched pillars supporting the
brick ceiling of the room stretch off into the gloom to the west.  There is a
case of chablis in the corner.  A small drain is set at floor level in the east
wall.

A panther is sitting on the floor here.


>x panther
Panthers aren't common in this part of the world, so you suspect that it must
have been imported from the far east.  Apparently uncle Wout felt his wine
cellar had to be guarded by an actual panther.

That panther seems hungry.  Perhaps it's been stuck in the cellar for a long
time.


>w
The panther won't let you.  It growls at you threateningly.


>give salmon to panther
The panther snatches the salmon from your hand and disappears into the gloom.

(Your score has just increased by one point.)

>w
West wine cellar
Korenvliet's wine cellar is large and musty.  Arched pillars supporting the
brick ceiling of the room stretch off into the gloom to the east.  A flight of
stairs leads up.

In the dim light, you see the sparkle of a crystal goblet sitting in a corner.


>take goblet
Taken.


>x goblet
It's a beautiful crystal goblet which must be quite valuable.  Even more
interestingly, there's a sticker glued to it on which the number "64" is
written.


>u
Top of stairs
You are at the top of a dimly lit flight of stairs going down.  The brick walls
here are cold and musty.  In the west wall is a small door.


>e
You can’t go that way.  Obvious exits lead west; and down, back to the west
wine cellar.


>unlock door
Unlocked.


>w
(first opening the cellar door)

Hallway
This short L-shaped hallway runs from a wooden door to the north to an open
archway to the west.  There is also a small door set in the east wall.  A large
portrait of uncle Wout with a wall safe behind it dominates the south wall.


>turn dial to 97
Okay, the dial is now set to 97.


>turn dial to 64
Okay, the dial is now set to 64.


>turn dial to 19
As you turn the dial to 19, a quiet click comes from the wall safe.

(Your score has just increased by one point.)

>open safe
Opening the wall safe reveals a will.


>read will
You read the document.  This is what it says:

*** LAST WILL AND TESTAMENT ***

I, Wout van Duysz ter Ghasth, in good health and with all my faculties, leave
all my possessions, including the Korenvliet estate, to whomever succeeds in
opening this safe.

Congratulations.

*** YOU HAVE WON ***

